+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent sets toolChoice to 'required', so after the supervisor declines approveRefund the model is forced to call a tool on every turn and can never produce the closing text reply, so it re-asks approval, re-looks-up the order, or runs out of maxTurns and fails.",
+  "evidence": "src/agents.ts:43 sets toolChoice: 'required' on refundAgent, and that config is applied through definePrompt/definePromptAgent (node_modules/@genkit-ai/ai/lib/agent.js:~800-830), so it governs every generate call in the agent loop. Its tools are only lookupOrder, approveRefund and issueRefund, so a forced tool call after a decline must be one of those, matching the three reported symptoms (re-asks approval, keeps working on the order, fails at maxTurns: 6). The triage agent at src/agents.ts:54 uses 'auto' and the decline path is not in the refund system prompt. Changed to 'auto'; npx tsc --noEmit passes. I did not run the flow live against Gemini."
+}
